 railways, metros, renewables and pipelines|Middle East (including Saudi Arabia and the UAE) - key growth region for transmission lines, substations and EHV cabling|Americas - United States, Mexico and Brazil (towers, poles and hardware through SAE Towers)|Africa - transmission and distribution, with reviving tendering activity|Commonwealth of Independent States (CIS)|SAARC region including Bangladesh and Nepal|Global presence across 110+ countries and 6 continents|Cables supplied to over 95 countries|Customers: Central and State Governments, Public Sector …","expansion":"To support future growth, KEC continues to strengthen its manufacturing and execution capabilities. It operates a global network of integrated manufacturing facilities and tower testing stations and has undertaken capacity expansions over the years across its key locations, including Dubai, Jaipur, Jabalpur and Butibori (Nagpur), along with capacity augmentation in Brazil; these investments are expected to enhance production capacity, improve supply chain responsiveness and support execution across large-scale projects. Alongside physical capacity, the Company is building out capability in …","grades":{"rel":0,"s":"","wm90":null},"industry":"Construction","isin":"INE389H01022","kpi":null,"listed_on":"","litigation":{"as_of":"","material":false,"note":"The routed profile text does not disclose any material litigation. It notes only that certain projects in Afghanistan earlier on hold due to a force majeure event have resumed execution under World Bank funding and that acknowledgement certificates were signed towards full and final settlement of dues on two ADB-funded projects."},"mdna":"India's cable and conductor market continues a structurally strong growth trajectory, driven by sustained public investment in power transmission and distribution, rapid scaling of renewable energy capacity, expanding 5G and fibre infrastructure, growing data centre ecosystems and accelerated railway modernisation.|S