ardware Supplies\"], \"Civil\": [\"Manufacturing & Process Plants\", \"Residential Buildings\", \"Airports\", \"Hospitals\", \"Water\", \"Commercial Buildings\", \"Data Centre\", \"Public Infrastructure\", \"Warehouse & Logistics\"], \"Transportation\": [\"Overhead Electrification\", \"Track Laying\", \"Tunnel Ventilation\", \"Signalling (ABS & Telecom)\", \"TCAS Kavach\", \"Railway Bridges\", \"Stations & Platforms\", \"Speed Upgradations\", \"Metro Viaduct, Station, Power Supply & …","promises":[],"promises_total":0,"promoters":[{"name":"Mr. Harsh V. Goenka","role":"Promoter Director; Non-Executive Chairman of the Board (DIN: 00026726)"}],"related":"[{\"name\": \"Al Sharif Group & KEC Limited Company\", \"relation\": \"subsidiary\", \"note\": \"51.10% held by the listed entity; participates in the Business Responsibility initiatives of the listed entity.\"}, {\"name\": \"KEC Asian Cables Limited\", \"relation\": \"subsidiary\", \"note\": \"100% held; India; …","risks":[{"note":"High dependence on a single geography may create concentration risk in growth, execution and recovery of receivables. The Company monitors geographic exposure - particularly in regions with heightened geopolitical uncertainty - through regular reviews of order book, order intake and project portfolio, places guardrails to limit overall exposure in a single geography and explores adequate insurance coverage.","risk":"Geography concentration"},{"note":"Political instability, regional conflicts, trade restrictions and policy changes in certain markets may disrupt supply chains, impact project execution and delay collections. Mitigation includes assessing the viability of continuing operations in affected regions, alternative strategic sourcing and evaluating ECGC and other suitable risk covers. Geopolitical tensions in the Middle East during Q4 FY26 were an explicitly flagged feature of the operating environment.","risk":"Geopolitical risk"},{"note":"Delays arising from right-of-way issues, land and forest clearances, challenging terrain, supply chain disruptions and labour availability may impact project execution, profitability and cash flows. Mitigation includes clear scope boundaries, tender contingency provisions, a shift toward mechanisation (crane-based tower erection, automated civil equipment) and a dynamic cost-compensation framework to re-negotiate project costs on unforeseen external delays.","risk":"Project execution risk"},{"note":"Exposure to fluctuations in prices of key commodities such as steel, zinc, copper and aluminium may impact project profitability. Mitigated by maintaining optimal hedge levels with central monitoring and periodic management review; in certain projects materials are supplied by the customer, who also bears price escalation.","risk":"Commodity price variation"},{"note":"Given the scale, complexity and duration of EPC projects, contractual disputes, claims and litigation may arise, potentially impacting project outcomes and financial performance. Mitigated by a structured contract review and approval process supported by dedicated legal and commercial teams, with learnings from past disputes fed into future negotiations.","risk":"Legal and contractual risk"},{"note":"Labour shortages were experienced by the industry throughout the year and constrained Civil revenues alongside delayed release of work fronts. Permanent-worker turnover rose to 39% in FY 2025-26 from 12% in FY 2024-25 (permanent employee turnover 25%), a structural execution constraint for a labour-intensive EPC model; the workforce strategy includes enhanced remuneration, upgraded labour amenities and a deliberate shift toward mechanisation.","risk":"Labour availability and workforce attrition"},{"note":"Identified in the BRSR materiality assessment as a risk: ensuring a safe workplace and continuity of operations across all verticals is critical to mitigating work-related injuries and illnesses and supporting uninterrupted project execution; safety incidents may reduce employee productivity and affect business deliverables. The Company has an EHS Policy and ISO 45001:2018 implemented across all business verticals.","risk":"Occupational health and safety"},{"note":"Identified in the BRSR materiality assessment as a risk: losing customers' confidence may impact the flow of new orders and hamper business growth. Mitigated through ISO 9001:2015 implemented across all verticals and a customer complaint redressal process with restricted resolution timelines.","risk":"Quality, service delivery and customer centricity"}],"rpt":{},"rpt_date":"","s":"KEC","sector":"Construction","sk":{"as_of":"2026-07-24","cagrs":[{"cagr":"4.81%","period":"2025-2030","segment":"Global Power EPC market"},{"cagr":"20.83%","period":"2025-2030","segment":"Indian Power EPC market"}],"drivers":"Government infrastructure push - Union Budget FY27 record capital expenditure outlay of Rs12.2 trillion|Integration of renewable energy (solar/wind) into the grid requiring new evacuation transmission|Grid strengthening, interconnection and modernisation (AIS/GIS substations, SCADA)|Underground …","industry":"Construction","market_size":[{"metric":"Global Power EPC market","value":"USD 201.97 billion","year":"2025E"},{"metric":"Global Power EPC market (projected)","value":"USD 255.45 billion","year":"2030P"},{"metric":"Indian Power EPC market","value":"USD 23.57 billion","year":"2025E"},{"metric":"Indian Power EPC market (projected)","value":"USD 60.72 billion","year":"2030P"},{"metric":"India gross electricity demand (CEA)","value":"approximately 1,694 TWh, up 17% from FY23 levels","year":"FY 2024-25"},{"metric":"India installed generation capacity","value":"crossed 475 GW; fossil fuels a little over half of total capacity, non-fossil (renewables, hydro, nuclear) the balance","year":"as of February 2026"},{"metric":"India transmission network at 220 kV and above","value":"~4.8-4.9 lakh circuit kilometers (ckm)","year":"as of early 2024"},{"metric":"Indi